// Regression guard: only `fn` DECLARATIONS hoist within a block. A VALUE binding (`total = 5`) stays
// strictly in source order even when nested, so referencing it before its assignment inside a fn body
// is still a runtime E0005 (unknown name) on both backends. This is what keeps hoisting fns past value
// bindings sound: fns are sealed and never read a surrounding value, so only the value's own
// order-dependence must be preserved.
// expect: error E0005 at 9:9
// expect: exit 1
fn outer(): int {
    x = total;   // used before its assignment below — still an error
    total = 5;
    return x;
}
echo outer();
